course: dictionary
lesson: 4937
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which one the writer means. «Real courts don't work like this — the writer is mocking judges who care most about their own importance.» Here, the judges care about how powerful or respected they seem, so importance means their status.
explain: Importance can also mean how much something matters. «The importance of wearing a helmet» is about how much a helmet matters to keep your head safe. Read the whole sentence before you decide which meaning fits.
explain: Use the swap test. Put your meaning into the sentence in place of the word and check that it still makes sense. If «how much it matters» fits, use that meaning. If the sentence is about a person's power or respect, try «how powerful or respected» instead.
fact: Importance is a noun, and it has no plural.
fact: «Importance» means how much something matters or how valuable it is.
fact: «Importance» can also mean how powerful or respected a person is, as in «a person of importance».
fact: «Of great importance» means very important, and «in order of importance» means ranked from most important to least important.
exercise: «Real courts don't work like this — the writer is mocking judges who care most about their own importance.» In this sentence, what does importance mean? | Being free of charge | Being a good cook | A very large building | *How powerful or respected a person thinks they are
exercise: Mum says, «Wearing a helmet is of great importance.» What does importance mean? | How heavy a helmet is | How many helmets there are | How loudly someone speaks | *How much it matters
exercise: Which phrase means ranked from the most important to the least important? | in order of colour | in order of height | *in order of importance | in order of noise
test: Which phrase means a person who is powerful or well respected? | a person in a hurry | a person of paint | *a person of importance | a person of few words
test: Teacher says, «We must stress the importance of reading.» What does stress the importance mean? | Write it in a different colour | Forget it completely | Say it very quietly | *Make clear how much it matters
exam: In «a person of importance», which meaning fits best? | *How powerful or respected someone is | How fast a car drives | How much rain fell that day | How soft a pillow feels
